<title>BELGIUM: It's all Greek to the Commission.</title>
<headline>It's all Greek to the Commission.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission has sent Greece a reasoned opinion for fixing the price of manufactured tobacco, according to a statement released on Thursday.</p>
<p>But there seemed to be some doubt about whether it was complaining about a minimum or a maximum price.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe that this should read &quot;maximum price&quot;, but have been unable to obtain confirmation of this from anybody,&quot; a translator's footnote to the statement said.</p>
<p>A Commission spokeswoman said &quot;minimum price&quot; was correct and that the translator's note was left there by mistake.</p>
<p>It is unclear whether any blame will attach to the unfortunate translator but Greece almost certainly faces the European Court of Justice if it does not scrap the practice within two months.</p>
</text>
